1
00:00:00,101 --> 00:00:02,137
I've already found
the woman you wanted me to look for.

2
00:00:02,137 --> 00:00:03,734
The woman named Joycelyn Trinidad.

3
00:00:03,734 --> 00:00:06,833
She's been a domestic helper in France
for 30 years.

4
00:00:06,834 --> 00:00:08,566
Is she the one you're looking for?

5
00:00:08,567 --> 00:00:09,299
No.

6
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:13,333
Maybe it's a blessing in disguise
if you lose your project in Blacksmith.

7
00:00:13,334 --> 00:00:14,900
Isn't that Savana?

8
00:00:14,901 --> 00:00:17,285
- Have you watched her video?
- Yes.

9
00:00:17,285 --> 00:00:19,354
She said a lot about her mother.

10
00:00:19,354 --> 00:00:21,222
Let's go somewhere else?

11
00:00:22,697 --> 00:00:24,565
Sorry.

12
00:00:27,478 --> 00:00:28,804
Where are we going?

13
00:00:28,805 --> 00:00:30,199
Looks like we're going on vacation.

14
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:31,533
It's just me.

15
00:00:31,534 --> 00:00:36,533
I'm used to traveling alone on my birthday.

16
00:00:36,534 --> 00:00:39,037
Is it because
I was busy with work in Casa Fuerte?

17
00:00:39,037 --> 00:00:42,307
If I say you'll return to Casa Fuerte,
you'll do as I say!

18
00:00:42,307 --> 00:00:43,526
Do you understand?

19
00:00:43,526 --> 00:00:46,878
Why does Uncle Ramon talk
as if he has more authority than dad?

20
00:00:46,878 --> 00:00:50,014
Have you forgotten about it?
We take care of his businesses.

21
00:00:50,014 --> 00:00:53,017
You can go against anyone
except Congressman Ramon.

22
00:00:53,017 --> 00:00:54,985
If you do, you'll get what you deserve.

23
00:01:05,596 --> 00:01:07,531
Let's go, girls.

24
00:01:38,463 --> 00:01:41,131
This. Let's try this.

25
00:01:45,470 --> 00:01:48,238
- I think this is better.
- Is that for me?

26
00:01:49,439 --> 00:01:50,999
Perfect timing.

27
00:01:50,999 --> 00:01:54,301
I think I need a massage.

28
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:57,815
You wish.

29
00:01:57,815 --> 00:01:59,484
You don't need a massage.

30
00:01:59,484 --> 00:02:02,653
Your bones need some twisting.

31
00:02:02,653 --> 00:02:04,322
You're so mean.

32
00:02:04,322 --> 00:02:06,391
You haven't changed a bit.

33
00:02:06,391 --> 00:02:08,626
You're still as violent.

34
00:02:08,626 --> 00:02:10,628
It's because of you.

35
00:02:10,628 --> 00:02:15,299
And what's stressing you out?
You get everything you want.

36
00:02:15,299 --> 00:02:19,138
Your son and I are the same.
We're both stubborn.

37
00:02:19,138 --> 00:02:21,938
Let me make this clear.

38
00:02:21,938 --> 00:02:24,542
Liam is happy with the film
he's making right now.

39
00:02:24,542 --> 00:02:29,346
If you can't support him,
just leave my son alone.

40
00:02:32,517 --> 00:02:34,652
Tess...

41
00:02:34,652 --> 00:02:37,810
Your son loves you so much.

42
00:02:37,810 --> 00:02:40,545
He will do everything for you.

43
00:02:44,429 --> 00:02:46,296
I'll just get this.

44
00:02:49,722 --> 00:02:51,903
This is for what she got.

45
00:02:51,903 --> 00:02:54,539
Didn't you get anything?

46
00:02:54,539 --> 00:02:57,441
You said it wouldn't work for me.

47
00:03:09,219 --> 00:03:10,487
[Records Section]

48
00:03:10,487 --> 00:03:13,540
Sir, here are Mrs. Teresita Buenaventura's
records.

49
00:03:13,540 --> 00:03:15,526
Thank you so much. Thank you.

50
00:03:15,526 --> 00:03:17,495
Please sign here.

51
00:03:17,495 --> 00:03:18,891
Sure.

52
00:03:19,831 --> 00:03:21,665
- Over here?
- Yeah.

53
00:03:22,667 --> 00:03:24,701
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

54
00:03:35,115 --> 00:03:37,334
Ten million pesos?

55
00:03:39,015 --> 00:03:41,868
<i>I paid this much money?</i>

56
00:03:41,868 --> 00:03:44,666
<i>How much do I make in Casa Fuerte?</i>

57
00:03:44,667 --> 00:03:46,073
<i>And what exactly is the job</i>

58
00:03:46,074 --> 00:03:49,429
<i>that I do for dad and Congressman Ramon?</i>

59
00:04:03,678 --> 00:04:05,767
<i>I'm sorry, the subscriber cannot be reached.</i>

60
00:04:05,767 --> 00:04:07,915
<i>Please try again later.</i>

61
00:04:07,915 --> 00:04:08,834
<i>I'm sorry, the sub...</i>

62
00:04:08,834 --> 00:04:10,167
[Call Ended]

63
00:04:10,167 --> 00:04:12,868
[Compose Message]
[To: Via]

64
00:04:12,868 --> 00:04:14,967
[Via, I just wanted to ask you something]

65
00:04:14,968 --> 00:04:17,067
[about my working relationship
with your dad.]

66
00:04:17,067 --> 00:04:20,300
[I will go see you at your office.]

67
00:04:27,761 --> 00:04:29,102
Great job today.

68
00:04:29,103 --> 00:04:30,704
Please include this one, too.

69
00:04:33,667 --> 00:04:35,902
Yeah, yeah. Bring it to the car.

70
00:04:43,176 --> 00:04:45,779
I want to thank you, Via.

71
00:04:45,779 --> 00:04:47,247
What for?

72
00:04:47,247 --> 00:04:50,467
For defending you?

73
00:04:50,467 --> 00:04:55,136
Or for the villains' wardrobe malfunction?

74
00:04:57,137 --> 00:04:59,192
Both.

75
00:04:59,192 --> 00:05:01,394
It's nothing.

76
00:05:01,394 --> 00:05:03,429
I'm your friend.

77
00:05:07,033 --> 00:05:08,868
Thank you...

78
00:05:10,603 --> 00:05:12,571
Because...

79
00:05:13,640 --> 00:05:15,975
I can feel...

80
00:05:15,975 --> 00:05:19,445
and see that you treat me as a friend.

81
00:05:21,981 --> 00:05:25,885
It's hard to find honest people in showbiz.

82
00:05:26,801 --> 00:05:28,824
Trust me, I know.

83
00:05:30,865 --> 00:05:38,063
Because I know... I can trust you.

84
00:05:41,002 --> 00:05:43,703
I'll be shameless this time, Via.

85
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:47,441
Can I...

86
00:05:49,043 --> 00:05:51,778
Can I ask you a favor?

87
00:05:54,949 --> 00:05:57,651
I'll be shameless this time, Via.

88
00:05:59,587 --> 00:06:01,388
Can I...

89
00:06:02,990 --> 00:06:05,593
Can I ask you a favor?

90
00:06:05,593 --> 00:06:06,954
Of course.

91
00:06:06,954 --> 00:06:08,728
What can I do for you?

92
00:06:10,463 --> 00:06:13,932
I want to have an interview in your magazine.

93
00:06:14,667 --> 00:06:16,335
Interview?

94
00:06:16,335 --> 00:06:18,204
About what?

95
00:06:20,231 --> 00:06:22,699
Let's just say that...

96
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:28,804
I want to clear the issues against me.

97
00:06:29,649 --> 00:06:38,157
My mom, who's a terror manager,
is so controlling.

98
00:06:38,157 --> 00:06:47,099
I'm like a goldfish placed in a tiny tank.

99
00:06:47,099 --> 00:06:51,804
Why can't she just flush me in the toilet?

100
00:06:53,207 --> 00:06:57,544
And you want to make decisions
for your life and career?

101
00:06:57,544 --> 00:07:01,215
If I let you decide for yourself,

102
00:07:01,215 --> 00:07:03,050
you would have lost your career already.

103
00:07:03,050 --> 00:07:04,885
You would have been pregnant.

104
00:07:04,885 --> 00:07:07,621
I should be the one to apologize.

105
00:07:07,621 --> 00:07:10,391
This has become our normal setup.

106
00:07:10,391 --> 00:07:13,716
You have to sneak just to see me.

107
00:07:13,716 --> 00:07:19,066
Maybe this is the sacrifice we have to make.

108
00:07:19,066 --> 00:07:22,403
If only I was a father
that you could introduce to people...

109
00:07:22,403 --> 00:07:23,404
Someone you could be proud of...

110
00:07:23,404 --> 00:07:25,672
Then you won't have a hard time.

111
00:07:28,876 --> 00:07:30,743
You know what?

112
00:07:31,712 --> 00:07:37,283
The photo shoot for our new campaign
is ongoing right now.

113
00:07:37,283 --> 00:07:40,886
We're calling it "Bare Naked",

114
00:07:40,886 --> 00:07:45,524
because the theme of the whole thing
is laying bare and stripping down.

115
00:07:45,524 --> 00:07:48,061
You know what I mean, like...

116
00:07:48,061 --> 00:07:53,666
No masks, no walls, just laying it all bare.

117
00:07:53,666 --> 00:07:55,534
Perfect.

118
00:07:56,803 --> 00:08:00,272
Are you ready to reveal everything?

119
00:08:02,175 --> 00:08:04,043
Yes...

120
00:08:05,011 --> 00:08:06,979
I'm ready.

121
00:08:15,555 --> 00:08:19,036
After that, let's take closer shots, okay?

122
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:29,902
Beautiful, I love it.

123
00:08:33,468 --> 00:08:35,971
I really like the eye makeup.

124
00:08:39,412 --> 00:08:41,559
More, more!

125
00:08:49,022 --> 00:08:50,924
Closer, please.

126
00:08:50,924 --> 00:08:53,893
Later. There, there. That's nice.

127
00:08:53,893 --> 00:08:55,795
- There.
- That's nice.

128
00:08:55,795 --> 00:08:57,930
Beautiful!

129
00:09:06,806 --> 00:09:08,781
Love!

130
00:09:08,781 --> 00:09:11,110
What are you doing here?

131
00:09:11,110 --> 00:09:13,880
I sent you a message,
but I don't think you've read it.

132
00:09:13,880 --> 00:09:16,473
Really? I'm so sorry.

133
00:09:16,473 --> 00:09:17,675
We're so busy.

134
00:09:17,675 --> 00:09:21,087
Look. Savana's photo shoot is still ongoing.

135
00:09:21,087 --> 00:09:22,511
Yeah.

136
00:09:52,502 --> 00:09:55,337
This is the first time I'm going to say this.

137
00:10:03,425 --> 00:10:07,328
I want to start by telling you
who I really am.

138
00:10:25,219 --> 00:10:28,355
The person you know...

139
00:10:31,025 --> 00:10:32,826
Savana...

140
00:10:39,901 --> 00:10:41,902
She's not who I really am.

141
00:10:48,257 --> 00:10:50,992
My real name is...

142
00:11:02,390 --> 00:11:04,825
Joycelyn Trinidad.

143
00:11:16,203 --> 00:11:17,838
I want...

144
00:11:22,255 --> 00:11:26,225
I want everyone to know me...

145
00:11:29,984 --> 00:11:32,052
as Joyce.

146
00:11:36,724 --> 00:11:38,959
The real me.

147
00:11:44,465 --> 00:11:46,133
Joyce...

148
00:11:49,904 --> 00:11:52,539
I realized...

149
00:11:53,893 --> 00:11:58,797
I realized that if I really
wanted to be a role model,

150
00:12:00,552 --> 00:12:04,321
I shouldn't be ashamed of who I really am.

151
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:09,618
And I won't be ashamed of where I came from.

152
00:12:19,266 --> 00:12:21,268
I was so drunk last night.

153
00:12:21,268 --> 00:12:23,270
Did I say something inappropriate?

154
00:12:23,270 --> 00:12:26,106
- Love?
- Joyce.

155
00:12:26,841 --> 00:12:28,909
Joyce?

156
00:12:31,273 --> 00:12:34,115
Joyce... Joycelyn Trinidad.

157
00:12:34,115 --> 00:12:36,249
Who is she?

158
00:12:40,673 --> 00:12:42,875
Excuse me. I'm sorry.

159
00:12:43,791 --> 00:12:45,759
Let's take a break.

160
00:12:47,728 --> 00:12:49,596
Let's take a break.

161
00:12:51,149 --> 00:12:52,583
Via!

162
00:13:35,543 --> 00:13:37,177
Miss Via?

163
00:13:43,417 --> 00:13:45,652
Are you okay?

164
00:14:01,869 --> 00:14:04,472
Miss Via, is it just a coincidence...

165
00:14:04,472 --> 00:14:10,610
or is Savana the Joycelyn Trinidad
you asked me to find?

166
00:14:16,050 --> 00:14:17,551
Love?

167
00:14:17,551 --> 00:14:20,053
Can you give us privacy first?

168
00:14:20,788 --> 00:14:23,189
I'll just give Savana a sponge bath.

169
00:14:24,558 --> 00:14:26,393
Via, what are you doing here?

170
00:14:26,393 --> 00:14:27,728
Surprise!

171
00:14:27,728 --> 00:14:29,563
I just thought I'd surprise you.

172
00:14:29,563 --> 00:14:30,564
I said leave!

173
00:14:30,564 --> 00:14:34,367
I'm not leaving because I love you!

174
00:14:37,438 --> 00:14:39,239
I think that's her.

175
00:14:42,586 --> 00:14:45,054
Why do you want me to find her?

176
00:14:47,915 --> 00:14:49,683
Queenie, get out.

177
00:14:49,683 --> 00:14:51,519
Get out.

178
00:14:51,519 --> 00:14:54,088
- Sorry.
- You don't have to know that.

179
00:14:54,088 --> 00:14:56,156
- Sorry.
- Out.

180
00:15:03,931 --> 00:15:05,932
Joyce.

181
00:15:08,269 --> 00:15:10,103
Joyce...

182
00:15:37,830 --> 00:15:39,867
Sir, everything's good now.

183
00:15:39,867 --> 00:15:41,368
Miss Savana, excuse me.

184
00:15:41,368 --> 00:15:42,936
Thank you.

185
00:15:45,573 --> 00:15:47,707
Are you worried yet?

186
00:15:48,709 --> 00:15:50,110
About what?

187
00:15:52,313 --> 00:15:55,115
Our film's billing.

188
00:15:56,649 --> 00:16:01,802
The posters will no longer
bear the name "Savana".

189
00:16:01,802 --> 00:16:03,412
It will be...

190
00:16:04,869 --> 00:16:06,626
"Joycelyn".

191
00:16:20,274 --> 00:16:24,210
Well, that's the least of my concerns.

192
00:16:24,945 --> 00:16:28,749
Your boyfriend told me
to take care of you, remember?

193
00:16:28,749 --> 00:16:30,316
Suitor.

194
00:16:31,418 --> 00:16:33,853
Hans and I are not together yet.

195
00:16:34,555 --> 00:16:37,724
I'm still trying to see
how patient he is in courting me.

196
00:16:40,761 --> 00:16:42,829
He might get tired.

197
00:16:47,534 --> 00:16:50,104
I hope he can wait.

198
00:16:50,104 --> 00:16:51,838
Wait?

199
00:16:54,241 --> 00:16:58,511
Wait until I'm ready to make
big decisions for myself.

200
00:16:59,980 --> 00:17:05,511
Well, I guess this is a good start.

201
00:17:05,511 --> 00:17:10,720
I mean, telling everyone
your real name, Joyce.

202
00:17:13,560 --> 00:17:15,095
Yes.

203
00:17:17,298 --> 00:17:21,936
Although I can retain
my screen name, Savana...

204
00:17:21,936 --> 00:17:24,037
I like Joyce better.

205
00:17:26,807 --> 00:17:31,811
I'm also happy that you've shown courage.

206
00:17:32,846 --> 00:17:36,617
I mean, the bashers can no longer use

207
00:17:36,617 --> 00:17:39,953
your too-good-to-be-true image against you.

208
00:18:10,818 --> 00:18:12,553
Believe it or not,

209
00:18:12,553 --> 00:18:15,945
I know how it feels to bottle up
everything inside.

210
00:18:18,492 --> 00:18:21,362
Maybe you need to do an interview with Via.

211
00:18:22,210 --> 00:18:23,677
Maybe you're right.

212
00:18:24,631 --> 00:18:26,300
Why, Liam?

213
00:18:26,300 --> 00:18:28,768
Do you also have something to confess?

214
00:18:30,237 --> 00:18:31,638
Via.

215
00:18:33,355 --> 00:18:34,806
Via.

216
00:18:38,912 --> 00:18:40,914
I'll let you know

217
00:18:40,914 --> 00:18:45,885
once the magazine publishes
your shoot and interview, Savana.

218
00:18:48,989 --> 00:18:50,456
I mean...

219
00:18:51,747 --> 00:18:53,414
Joyce.

220
00:18:55,329 --> 00:18:57,964
Via, thank you so much.

221
00:19:12,246 --> 00:19:15,748
You said you have something to tell me.

222
00:19:17,518 --> 00:19:20,420
Yes, Via.
There's something I need to tell you.

223
00:19:21,855 --> 00:19:23,924
So, Savana...

224
00:19:23,924 --> 00:19:25,859
Joyce.

225
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:35,501
I'll go ahead, Joyce.

226
00:20:05,265 --> 00:20:06,799
Via...

227
00:20:07,801 --> 00:20:10,471
About my...

228
00:20:10,471 --> 00:20:12,872
question...

229
00:20:15,342 --> 00:20:19,379
This is about my working relationship
with your dad.

230
00:20:20,739 --> 00:20:23,975
Because of everything
that has happened lately,

231
00:20:25,419 --> 00:20:27,988
I'm just worried that
I might not be able to fulfill

232
00:20:27,988 --> 00:20:30,390
some of my obligations to him.

233
00:20:32,793 --> 00:20:36,163
You know that as much as possible,

234
00:20:36,163 --> 00:20:40,767
I don't meddle with my dad's businesses.

235
00:20:40,767 --> 00:20:42,151
Because?

236
00:20:42,151 --> 00:20:43,952
Because he doesn't like it.

237
00:20:46,377 --> 00:20:48,945
That's one thing you both agree on, right?

238
00:20:50,231 --> 00:20:53,133
You don't want anyone
interfering with your life.

239
00:20:59,286 --> 00:21:01,989
Do we have a problem, Via?

240
00:21:07,161 --> 00:21:09,016
You tell me...

241
00:21:09,016 --> 00:21:10,483
Love.

242
00:21:11,865 --> 00:21:14,534
Is there something I need to worry about?

243
00:22:14,259 --> 00:22:15,921
Mommy?

244
00:22:22,965 --> 00:22:24,533
Sweetie...

245
00:22:26,630 --> 00:22:29,943
I hope you understand...

246
00:22:29,943 --> 00:22:34,747
that everything I do is for you.

247
00:22:37,069 --> 00:22:38,903
Yes, Mommy.

248
00:22:40,621 --> 00:22:43,856
I don't forget that.

249
00:22:55,172 --> 00:22:58,475
I want to tell you something.

250
00:23:02,909 --> 00:23:07,314
I don't want to hear it
if it's not good news.

251
00:23:07,314 --> 00:23:09,816
What is it? New project?

252
00:23:09,816 --> 00:23:12,952
New endorsement? Or an award?

253
00:23:17,896 --> 00:23:22,133
Mommy, I just want to tell you...

254
00:23:26,700 --> 00:23:29,436
I just want to tell you
that I love you so much.

255
00:23:29,436 --> 00:23:32,905
And I will never intend...

256
00:23:34,044 --> 00:23:36,913
to hurt you or make you suffer.

257
00:23:42,145 --> 00:23:44,380
I thought you were going
to say something else.

258
00:23:59,333 --> 00:24:01,702
Good night, Mommy.

259
00:24:01,702 --> 00:24:04,170
Okay, good night.

260
00:25:27,320 --> 00:25:29,890
Maybe you're tired.

261
00:25:29,890 --> 00:25:33,293
Maybe this is not the right time to ask.

262
00:25:33,293 --> 00:25:37,964
I'll just ask you next time.

263
00:25:39,566 --> 00:25:40,967
Wait, Love.

264
00:25:40,967 --> 00:25:42,569
Sorry. Sorry.

265
00:25:45,172 --> 00:25:48,442
I just have a lot on my mind.

266
00:25:48,442 --> 00:25:50,744
I'm sorry.
Okay, what do you want to talk about?

267
00:25:50,744 --> 00:25:52,913
It's okay, it's okay.

268
00:25:52,913 --> 00:25:55,749
I'm sorry for bothering you.

269
00:25:55,749 --> 00:26:00,386
Maybe I should just drive you home.

270
00:26:09,367 --> 00:26:11,700
[Girl with Periwinkle Hair]
<i>Hello, friends!</i>

271
00:26:11,701 --> 00:26:15,738
<i>It's me again,
your trusted showbiz authority,</i>

272
00:26:15,738 --> 00:26:19,542
<i>the Girl with the Periwinkle Hair!</i>

273
00:26:19,542 --> 00:26:24,383
<i>Well, it takes a great actress
to portray challenging roles.</i>

274
00:26:24,383 --> 00:26:31,666
<i>But a great level of acting is needed
to pretend to be someone you're not.</i>

275
00:26:31,667 --> 00:26:34,737
<i>Well, I'm talking about this famous actress</i>

276
00:26:34,737 --> 00:26:37,807
<i>who just revealed her true identity.</i>

277
00:26:37,807 --> 00:26:43,666
<i>Apparently, the image she has
all these years,</i>

278
00:26:43,667 --> 00:26:47,905
<i>like the roles she took, is fake.</i>

279
00:26:47,905 --> 00:26:50,875
<i>Fictional, made-up, manufactured!</i>

280
00:26:50,875 --> 00:26:54,545
<i>The actress I'm talking about
is none other than,</i>

281
00:26:54,545 --> 00:26:57,815
<i>your favorite and most in-demand, Savana.</i>

282
00:26:57,815 --> 00:27:02,219
<i>She's introducing herself now
as Joycelyn Trinidad.</i>

283
00:27:02,219 --> 00:27:04,794
<i>And according to my sources,</i>

284
00:27:04,794 --> 00:27:12,429
<i>she hid her true identity
because of a deep, dark secret</i>

285
00:27:12,429 --> 00:27:15,599
<i>involving her past and her family.</i>

286
00:27:15,599 --> 00:27:19,603
<i>Her father is drug-dependent</i>

287
00:27:19,603 --> 00:27:23,240
<i>who even went to jail
because of a drug-related crime.</i>

288
00:27:23,240 --> 00:27:25,242
<i>Oh, poor Savana.</i>

289
00:27:25,242 --> 00:27:27,011
<i>Or should I say...</i>

290
00:27:27,011 --> 00:27:29,534
- This is why I prefer independent films.
- <i>poor Joyce...</i>

291
00:27:29,534 --> 00:27:31,167
Come on, Leroy!

292
00:27:31,167 --> 00:27:34,084
Can't you give Savana a little sympathy?

293
00:27:34,084 --> 00:27:36,387
I feel bad for her.

294
00:27:36,387 --> 00:27:40,090
I know how it feels when
the whole world against you.

295
00:27:41,425 --> 00:27:46,030
It reminds me of my husband's family.

296
00:27:46,030 --> 00:27:47,865
Calm down, Miss Megan.

297
00:27:47,865 --> 00:27:50,968
You look so affected.

298
00:27:50,968 --> 00:27:56,740
<i>Or maybe the real victim here is her father.</i>

299
00:28:05,215 --> 00:28:06,767
Boss Bro?

300
00:28:06,767 --> 00:28:08,618
Have you seen the latest video about Savana

301
00:28:08,618 --> 00:28:12,422
by the Girl with Periwinkle Hair?

302
00:28:12,422 --> 00:28:14,424
I'm watching it now, Borj.

303
00:28:14,424 --> 00:28:15,758
Bye.

304
00:28:19,763 --> 00:28:21,231
<i>What kind of a daughter</i>

305
00:28:21,231 --> 00:28:27,070
<i>can forsake her own father
for fame and money?</i>

306
00:28:27,070 --> 00:28:28,704
Joyce...

307
00:28:29,906 --> 00:28:34,510
Who in the world is behind that?

308
00:28:35,245 --> 00:28:38,748
I didn't know Savana's real name is Joycelyn.

309
00:28:40,701 --> 00:28:45,006
Why does Joycelyn seem familiar to me?

310
00:28:45,006 --> 00:28:46,940
Joyce?

311
00:28:48,073 --> 00:28:49,708
Joyce...

312
00:28:56,017 --> 00:29:03,057
<i>Maybe that's how it really is
when you turn yourself into a commodity.</i>

313
00:29:03,057 --> 00:29:07,528
<i>So friends, be careful who you look up to.</i>

314
00:29:07,528 --> 00:29:09,933
<i>Bye for now.</i>

315
00:29:09,934 --> 00:29:13,067
<i>This is your trusted showbiz authority,</i>

316
00:29:13,067 --> 00:29:17,133
<i>the Girl with the Periwinkle Hair!</i>

317
00:29:17,133 --> 00:29:19,206
<i>Bye!</i>

318
00:29:30,184 --> 00:29:32,219
Savana!

319
00:29:32,887 --> 00:29:35,701
Savana, what did you do?

320
00:29:35,701 --> 00:29:37,316
What did you do?

321
00:29:37,316 --> 00:29:41,121
Who did you tell about your real name?

322
00:29:41,122 --> 00:29:42,890
Who?

323
00:29:44,699 --> 00:29:50,337
I... I only told one person, Mommy.

324
00:29:56,711 --> 00:29:59,079
Come on, Savana!

325
00:30:15,763 --> 00:30:16,964
Where's your boss?

326
00:30:16,964 --> 00:30:19,900
- Miss Via is in an important meeting.
- Excuse me.

327
00:30:23,971 --> 00:30:26,239
Can we talk?

328
00:30:27,308 --> 00:30:28,909
Girls.

329
00:30:33,414 --> 00:30:37,885
- Savana, what are you doing?
- Don't deny it, Via.

330
00:30:37,885 --> 00:30:41,655
I thought we were friends.
But what did you do?

331
00:30:41,655 --> 00:30:43,224
I don't know what you're talking about.

332
00:30:43,224 --> 00:30:45,625
Please, just admit it!

333
00:30:46,293 --> 00:30:47,726
Admit what?

334
00:30:47,726 --> 00:30:51,599
What is going on?

335
00:30:51,599 --> 00:30:54,235
Get back to work. Back to work. Go!

336
00:30:54,235 --> 00:30:59,507
How convenient is it
that after I told you about my real name,

337
00:30:59,507 --> 00:31:01,809
the Girl with Periwinkle Hair came out
with a video about me

338
00:31:01,809 --> 00:31:02,834
and even dragged my father into it!

339
00:31:02,834 --> 00:31:05,746
My whole life is now out in the open!

340
00:31:05,746 --> 00:31:07,567
Wait, what? I'm sorry...

341
00:31:07,567 --> 00:31:10,518
Via, I just realized...

342
00:31:10,518 --> 00:31:14,155
You only defended me from Maxine

343
00:31:14,155 --> 00:31:16,456
so I would trust you.

344
00:31:23,097 --> 00:31:28,134
You really think
I'm behind that malicious content?

345
00:31:33,100 --> 00:31:35,100
[I Am Joyce]

346
00:31:37,701 --> 00:31:44,501
[I Am Joyce]

347
00:31:45,429 --> 00:31:47,388
Savana...

348
00:31:47,388 --> 00:31:50,323
or should I call you Joyce?

349
00:31:52,193 --> 00:31:54,995
I admired what you did.

350
00:31:55,980 --> 00:31:56,982
I even told my team

351
00:31:56,982 --> 00:32:00,719
to rush and include this article
in our latest issue.

352
00:32:00,721 --> 00:32:03,423
I didn't sleep just to write it.

353
00:32:04,238 --> 00:32:11,211
And I swear I really did my best
to write it as fair as I can.

354
00:32:13,681 --> 00:32:15,649
It's beyond my control, Savana.

355
00:32:15,649 --> 00:32:17,051
I have no control over people's minds

356
00:32:17,051 --> 00:32:20,720
if they will put malice
to what you confessed, okay?

357
00:32:22,256 --> 00:32:25,825
I don't get you.
What are you talking about now?

358
00:32:32,700 --> 00:32:36,537
Via, I... I'm sorry.

359
00:32:36,537 --> 00:32:38,471
I'm sorry, I thought...

360
00:32:39,773 --> 00:32:44,588
I thought you were the only one
who knew about it.

361
00:32:44,588 --> 00:32:49,182
I didn't know
that you already published the article.

362
00:32:50,184 --> 00:32:54,150
I'm sorry, Via.
I just can't bear all the bashing.

363
00:32:57,291 --> 00:32:59,059
Just take it.

364
00:33:00,948 --> 00:33:05,285
Sorry, Joyce, just... get out of my office.

365
00:33:08,969 --> 00:33:10,437
Just go.

366
00:33:29,078 --> 00:33:31,013
Hello, Dad?

367
00:33:35,829 --> 00:33:38,431
Okay, Dad. I'm on my way there.

368
00:33:41,101 --> 00:33:42,536
Liam?

369
00:33:42,536 --> 00:33:46,231
Because of the new issue about Savana,

370
00:33:46,231 --> 00:33:49,443
or should I call her Joyce...

371
00:33:49,443 --> 00:33:52,612
We decided to pull her out of Josh's movie.

372
00:33:53,881 --> 00:33:55,952
Wait, why?

373
00:33:55,952 --> 00:33:57,951
Do we already know the truth?

374
00:33:59,486 --> 00:34:01,522
What do you mean by truth?

375
00:34:01,522 --> 00:34:03,800
Liam, in this industry,

376
00:34:03,800 --> 00:34:06,961
nothing is more important than
people's perceptions.

377
00:34:06,961 --> 00:34:08,829
Savana is so ruined

378
00:34:08,829 --> 00:34:14,201
because a lot of people
are malicious and gullible like you.

379
00:34:14,201 --> 00:34:15,502
What did you say?

380
00:34:15,502 --> 00:34:17,838
Stop, you two!

381
00:34:17,838 --> 00:34:22,009
Liam, you can defend Savana or Joyce
all you want.

382
00:34:22,009 --> 00:34:28,983
But this issue regarding her
ex-con and drug-dependent father,

383
00:34:28,983 --> 00:34:34,021
and the fact that Savana hid it
because she's ashamed of him?

384
00:34:34,021 --> 00:34:38,625
This will cause serious damage
to the film she's doing with Josh.

385
00:34:38,625 --> 00:34:39,793
Sorry, Liam.

386
00:34:39,793 --> 00:34:42,196
I want to win the elections.

387
00:34:42,196 --> 00:34:44,498
I don't want any more trouble.

388
00:34:44,498 --> 00:34:47,067
I want you to release my movie
before the campaign period,

389
00:34:47,067 --> 00:34:50,270
which is a couple of months from now.

390
00:34:53,307 --> 00:34:56,843
Don't we care about anything
but our own agenda?

391
00:34:58,245 --> 00:35:00,347
You should pity Joyce.

392
00:35:00,347 --> 00:35:05,319
Everyone's critical of her,
and now you're letting her down?

393
00:35:05,319 --> 00:35:07,721
You can laugh at our reason.

394
00:35:07,721 --> 00:35:11,924
But I'm not going to produce a film
with a problematic actress.

395
00:35:11,924 --> 00:35:15,695
Josh's role is a public servant.

396
00:35:15,695 --> 00:35:18,463
You don't expect him to have
a rebellious leading lady?

397
00:35:19,165 --> 00:35:21,300
Is that really the reason?

398
00:35:24,470 --> 00:35:26,973
Uncle Ramon, can you say something?

399
00:35:26,973 --> 00:35:29,274
You did tell me something, remember?

400
00:35:29,942 --> 00:35:31,377
Liam...

401
00:35:31,377 --> 00:35:33,278
Watch your mouth, Liam.

402
00:35:35,007 --> 00:35:38,442
Why don't you just tell the truth?

403
00:35:39,785 --> 00:35:44,123
Joyce is getting caught in between,

404
00:35:44,123 --> 00:35:49,362
and my film is delayed
because you have a problem with me.

405
00:35:49,362 --> 00:35:53,199
The truth is, you want me out of this project

406
00:35:53,199 --> 00:35:56,935
so I can go back and work for you.

407
00:35:57,803 --> 00:36:01,507
I know how much I owe Casa Fuerte.

408
00:36:01,507 --> 00:36:05,845
And you're making me pay it back
by making me do things.

409
00:36:05,845 --> 00:36:08,181
Well, let's do this.

410
00:36:08,181 --> 00:36:13,052
You can pull me out of this project,
but you must retain Joyce.

411
00:36:13,052 --> 00:36:14,520
Liam, will you shut up?

412
00:36:14,520 --> 00:36:16,188
All right.

413
00:36:25,198 --> 00:36:27,032
You said it yourself.

414
00:36:28,034 --> 00:36:31,737
Joyce, A.K.A. Savana,

415
00:36:31,737 --> 00:36:37,843
will stay in this project
if you return to Casa Fuerte.

416
00:37:00,466 --> 00:37:02,072
My friend.

417
00:37:02,072 --> 00:37:05,475
I apologize for what my son did.

418
00:37:33,966 --> 00:37:38,403
Mr. Trinidad, we only want to hear your side.

419
00:37:39,071 --> 00:37:41,440
Does Edmond Trinidad live here?

420
00:37:41,440 --> 00:37:44,443
Savana's father? Yes, he lives here.

421
00:37:44,443 --> 00:37:49,148
Mr. Trinidad, we only want to make it clear.

422
00:37:49,148 --> 00:37:55,821
Savana, I mean, Joyce,
is now in the hot seat.

423
00:37:55,821 --> 00:38:01,412
Did she hide her real identity
because she's ashamed of you?

424
00:38:04,297 --> 00:38:06,299
She's a bad woman!

425
00:38:06,299 --> 00:38:07,700
Savana's here!

426
00:38:07,700 --> 00:38:08,993
Her name's Joyce!

427
00:38:08,993 --> 00:38:11,361
She's here. Take a video.

428
00:38:19,178 --> 00:38:21,380
Leave her alone!

429
00:38:21,380 --> 00:38:23,281
Leeches!

430
00:38:27,804 --> 00:38:29,339
Please stop.

431
00:38:30,742 --> 00:38:32,792
That's enough. Talk to me.

432
00:38:32,792 --> 00:38:35,461
Mr. Trinidad, just give us something.

433
00:38:35,461 --> 00:38:38,363
Is it true, Savana,
that you changed your name?

434
00:38:39,485 --> 00:38:42,654
I thought about it carefully before I did it.

435
00:38:44,036 --> 00:38:46,305
When I confess my real name,

436
00:38:46,305 --> 00:38:50,213
I know a lot will be revealed about my life.

437
00:38:51,544 --> 00:38:53,879
And I accept all that.

438
00:38:55,280 --> 00:38:59,051
I accept that a lot of you
will be disappointed.

439
00:38:59,051 --> 00:39:02,320
I accept that a lot will turn their backs.

440
00:39:06,425 --> 00:39:08,527
But I'm begging you. Talk to me instead.

441
00:39:08,527 --> 00:39:10,996
Keep my loved ones out of it.

442
00:39:10,996 --> 00:39:14,835
Especially my father,
because I love him so much.

443
00:39:18,616 --> 00:39:21,485
My dad and I are doing fine.

444
00:39:22,875 --> 00:39:25,611
I'm begging you,
don't drag my family into this.

445
00:39:25,611 --> 00:39:30,015
I can afford to lose everything
except my loved ones.

446
00:39:32,451 --> 00:39:34,527
- Oh, come on.
- That's just drama.

447
00:39:34,527 --> 00:39:36,628
She's just being defensive.

448
00:39:37,923 --> 00:39:42,060
- Should we believe that?
- Is it true?

449
00:39:42,795 --> 00:39:44,430
- Do you believe it?
- We won't believe it!

450
00:39:44,430 --> 00:39:47,566
Mr. Trinidad, please give a short statement.

451
00:39:54,039 --> 00:39:56,642
Get out of my property!

452
00:39:56,642 --> 00:39:59,111
- Mommy!
- Get out of here! The show is over!

453
00:39:59,111 --> 00:40:01,280
It's over! Get lost!

454
00:40:01,280 --> 00:40:03,916
- Joanne.
- Get lost!

455
00:40:03,916 --> 00:40:05,951
Get out of here!

456
00:40:09,088 --> 00:40:10,256
Sorry, Auntie.

457
00:40:10,256 --> 00:40:11,824
- Mom?
- It's okay.

458
00:40:11,824 --> 00:40:15,060
Son? We're here in the kitchen.

459
00:40:17,496 --> 00:40:18,931
Via?

460
00:40:18,931 --> 00:40:20,365
What happened?

461
00:40:21,986 --> 00:40:25,673
Savana fought with Via.

462
00:40:25,673 --> 00:40:27,266
Savana barged into her office

463
00:40:27,266 --> 00:40:30,810
and accused her that she is the Girl with...

464
00:40:30,810 --> 00:40:32,778
What's the color of her hair again?

465
00:40:32,778 --> 00:40:34,647
Violet, purple...

466
00:40:34,647 --> 00:40:35,981
Periwinkle!

467
00:40:35,981 --> 00:40:37,416
That's it.

468
00:40:38,584 --> 00:40:40,319
It was...

469
00:40:40,319 --> 00:40:43,355
It was because of my interview with her.

470
00:40:43,355 --> 00:40:46,525
She told me her real name, remember?

471
00:40:46,525 --> 00:40:49,566
It was so easy for her to assume

472
00:40:49,566 --> 00:40:53,799
that I was the one who revealed
the issue of her family.

473
00:40:53,799 --> 00:40:56,089
I didn't do anything like that.

474
00:40:56,089 --> 00:41:02,807
She said I'm the online bully
who does nothing good in life.

475
00:41:07,014 --> 00:41:08,642
Via...

476
00:41:09,460 --> 00:41:15,732
Via, I'm sorry if you got offended, but...

477
00:41:18,557 --> 00:41:20,158
But what?

478
00:41:24,718 --> 00:41:26,419
But maybe you should try...

479
00:41:27,470 --> 00:41:30,372
putting yourself in her shoes.

480
00:41:32,538 --> 00:41:34,172
I mean...

481
00:41:35,407 --> 00:41:38,377
I know what she did was wrong.

482
00:41:38,377 --> 00:41:41,627
But because of what she's going through...

483
00:41:41,627 --> 00:41:46,097
maybe we should understand
why she's careless.

484
00:41:52,691 --> 00:41:54,526
Excuse me.

485
00:41:56,695 --> 00:41:59,197
- Auntie, thank you.
- Dear...

486
00:42:00,900 --> 00:42:02,234
- Thank you.
- Via, my dear.

487
00:42:02,234 --> 00:42:04,069
Via, wait.

488
00:42:04,737 --> 00:42:06,363
Sorry, Liam.

489
00:42:07,398 --> 00:42:11,511
I didn't know that problems
have a hierarchy...

490
00:42:11,511 --> 00:42:14,214
That Joyce is going through something worse,

491
00:42:14,214 --> 00:42:16,849
than what she did to me?

492
00:42:18,051 --> 00:42:19,719
My gosh.

493
00:42:19,719 --> 00:42:22,522
Sorry for coming here.

494
00:42:22,522 --> 00:42:25,624
I thought you would be on my side.

495
00:42:35,134 --> 00:42:36,435
Mom...

496
00:42:38,137 --> 00:42:39,872
Was I wrong?

497
00:42:41,875 --> 00:42:45,611
Liam, it's not about being right or wrong.

498
00:42:47,059 --> 00:42:49,795
Via is your girlfriend.

499
00:42:56,890 --> 00:43:02,861
Liam, dear, listen to me.
This is the only time I will talk about this.

500
00:43:03,496 --> 00:43:04,998
Son...

501
00:43:04,998 --> 00:43:12,108
You know about everything I had been through
because of your dad.

502
00:43:13,866 --> 00:43:17,869
You know every pain I went through

503
00:43:17,869 --> 00:43:21,171
because he couldn't stand by me.

504
00:43:24,083 --> 00:43:27,986
Liam, son, don't be like Danilo.

505
00:43:28,919 --> 00:43:32,956
Don't treat Via like how your dad treated me.

506
00:43:34,715 --> 00:43:39,419
Now, if there's someone that matters
more to you, Liam.

507
00:43:41,634 --> 00:43:43,235
Son...

508
00:43:44,237 --> 00:43:45,972
Man up.

509
00:43:45,972 --> 00:43:48,407
Admit the truth...

510
00:43:49,208 --> 00:43:51,276
to yourself...

511
00:43:52,078 --> 00:43:56,582
and to the person you can possibly hurt.

512
00:44:12,465 --> 00:44:13,889
My dear,

513
00:44:13,889 --> 00:44:20,640
please find out which network
sent those reporters to Edmond's house.

514
00:44:20,640 --> 00:44:25,311
Get me an appointment with them, please?

515
00:44:25,311 --> 00:44:26,912
Okay, bye.

516
00:44:32,986 --> 00:44:38,123
Dear, don't take this the wrong way.

517
00:44:38,825 --> 00:44:42,127
But you need to listen to your mom.

518
00:44:43,262 --> 00:44:45,164
I'm glad...

519
00:44:45,164 --> 00:44:49,035
that you were able to tell the world
who you really are.

520
00:44:49,035 --> 00:44:53,172
Your real name, the life you had...

521
00:44:54,974 --> 00:44:59,946
But it's true that...
I'm the one who did wrong.

522
00:44:59,946 --> 00:45:04,450
And I can't bear it, Joyce...

523
00:45:04,450 --> 00:45:10,189
if you and your mom will lose
everything you worked hard for.

524
00:45:10,189 --> 00:45:13,159
Just because of me.

525
00:45:13,159 --> 00:45:14,493
Dad...

526
00:45:16,162 --> 00:45:18,231
Listen to your mom.

527
00:45:18,231 --> 00:45:22,034
She won't do anything that can harm you.

528
00:45:24,737 --> 00:45:26,271
And...

529
00:45:27,707 --> 00:45:30,008
don't worry about me.

530
00:45:31,878 --> 00:45:33,479
I can handle this.

531
00:46:09,817 --> 00:46:11,351
Joyce...

532
00:46:13,252 --> 00:46:16,956
I'm at this point in my life again...

533
00:46:16,956 --> 00:46:20,226
that I have to make a big decision.

534
00:46:25,031 --> 00:46:28,033
They want me back in Casa Fuerte...

535
00:46:29,769 --> 00:46:32,671
Back to the life I thought I wanted.

536
00:46:37,310 --> 00:46:39,378
You know what, Joyce?

537
00:46:40,613 --> 00:46:43,115
Only one thing is clear.

538
00:46:45,653 --> 00:46:51,525
That I should not do what I did
with the typewriter.

539
00:46:53,593 --> 00:46:55,894
I shouldn't be selfish.

540
00:46:59,732 --> 00:47:01,733
Joyce, you should...

541
00:47:02,668 --> 00:47:05,270
finish your dream project.

542
00:47:06,806 --> 00:47:08,740
Maybe...

543
00:47:10,910 --> 00:47:13,245
this is only right.

544
00:47:14,747 --> 00:47:17,282
Because other people are getting hurt, too.

545
00:47:21,254 --> 00:47:24,056
So even though I was so...

546
00:47:26,692 --> 00:47:29,662
I was so happy...

547
00:47:29,662 --> 00:47:33,498
to be with you again...

548
00:47:37,937 --> 00:47:41,207
Even though I thought...

549
00:47:41,207 --> 00:47:44,743
we could fulfill our dreams together.

550
00:47:45,545 --> 00:47:48,276
Even if it's hard...

551
00:47:48,276 --> 00:47:50,415
Who said it was easy?

552
00:47:56,464 --> 00:47:58,291
You're already making it a habit.

553
00:47:58,291 --> 00:48:00,827
You only come to me when you have a problem.

554
00:48:00,827 --> 00:48:03,129
I don't come here to see you.

555
00:48:03,129 --> 00:48:04,463
Her.

556
00:48:06,532 --> 00:48:09,201
Would you rather talk to her than me?

557
00:48:13,139 --> 00:48:18,877
Bro, life is an endless cycle
of making choices.

558
00:48:20,213 --> 00:48:22,048
Like the junk I scavenged.

559
00:48:22,048 --> 00:48:24,684
Most of them are useless.

560
00:48:24,684 --> 00:48:27,686
But it will surprise you...

561
00:48:29,000 --> 00:48:30,797
because they can still be used.

562
00:48:30,797 --> 00:48:32,190
See?

563
00:48:34,093 --> 00:48:36,628
What if I tell you that...

564
00:48:37,363 --> 00:48:39,031
this is not the life I chose?

565
00:48:39,031 --> 00:48:41,334
What do you mean you didn't choose this?

566
00:48:41,334 --> 00:48:43,169
Come on, bro.

567
00:48:43,169 --> 00:48:46,072
That is what's wrong in our society.

568
00:48:46,072 --> 00:48:48,541
People suffer...

569
00:48:48,541 --> 00:48:53,379
because decisions are made by people

570
00:48:53,379 --> 00:48:56,249
who won't own up to their mistakes.

571
00:48:56,249 --> 00:48:57,884
Bro...

572
00:48:57,884 --> 00:49:02,088
People need to learn how to
take responsibility for their decisions.

573
00:49:02,088 --> 00:49:06,926
I regret a lot of the decisions I made.

574
00:49:06,926 --> 00:49:10,296
That's why I have this kind of life.

575
00:49:10,296 --> 00:49:13,765
But I'm already here. What else can I do?

576
00:49:14,533 --> 00:49:16,035
That's why I deal with it.

577
00:49:16,035 --> 00:49:17,803
I endure it.

578
00:49:17,803 --> 00:49:22,040
I stand by it.
Because I can't blame anyone but myself.

579
00:49:23,943 --> 00:49:27,480
What was the wrong decision you made?

580
00:49:27,480 --> 00:49:31,103
That's the problem. I can't remember anymore.

581
00:49:34,987 --> 00:49:39,392
But, bro, the important question is...

582
00:49:39,392 --> 00:49:40,759
How about you?

583
00:49:41,627 --> 00:49:45,464
What mistake you made should you face?

584
00:50:07,353 --> 00:50:10,022
Stefano Lualhati is his real name.

585
00:50:10,022 --> 00:50:11,490
He was from Verde Village.

586
00:50:11,490 --> 00:50:12,558
Verde Village?

587
00:50:12,558 --> 00:50:15,728
Why, Liam? Do you know the kid's parents?

588
00:50:15,728 --> 00:50:19,598
Liam, regarding Savana's action scenes.

589
00:50:19,598 --> 00:50:21,334
I hope you take care of her.

590
00:50:21,334 --> 00:50:23,635
I mean, Joyce.

591
00:50:23,635 --> 00:50:26,539
Sorry, I'm not used to calling you Joyce.

592
00:50:26,539 --> 00:50:29,875
Liam is so used to calling her Joyce.

593
00:50:29,875 --> 00:50:32,078
- Actually, Via...
- Can I talk to you?

594
00:50:32,078 --> 00:50:34,046
Hans, just so you know,

595
00:50:34,046 --> 00:50:36,716
Liam is not working at Blacksmith anymore.

596
00:50:36,716 --> 00:50:38,517
He'll return to Casa Fuerte.

597
00:50:38,517 --> 00:50:39,917
What about our movie?

598
00:50:39,917 --> 00:50:45,825
We have established by now
that my boyfriend has a lot of secrets.

599
00:50:45,825 --> 00:50:48,627
Is Via still mad at me?

600
00:50:48,627 --> 00:50:50,680
I'm sorry.

601
00:50:50,680 --> 00:50:52,974
So she's still mad at me.

602
00:50:52,974 --> 00:50:54,800
Don't blame yourself.

603
00:50:54,800 --> 00:50:58,337
I don't have anyone else to blame but me.

604
00:50:58,337 --> 00:51:00,673
I think that is what you should do too.

605
00:51:00,673 --> 00:51:03,342
Take full accountability
for all your decisions.

606
00:51:03,342 --> 00:51:05,757
I want to apologize to you.

607
00:51:05,757 --> 00:51:07,918
I know I did wrong.

608
00:51:07,918 --> 00:51:11,783
I told Liam
that I was not ready yet to see you.
